A process holds its table by a node that is a root rather than one below the CapTable capability,
so revoking that capability, or destroying the table's pool, does not take it;
every capability to an object lies below its pool's own node.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: capability to an object is a root

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -313,7 +313,7 @@ static int op_pool(struct thread *t, uint32_t slot, const struct cap *cap,
         }
         /* It hangs below the capability it was made with, so a revoke above that takes it. */
         proc->table = tc;
-        cap_attach(slot_node(t, arg[3]), &proc->table);
+        cap_attach(NULL, &proc->table);
         obj = &proc->hdr;
         break;
     }
